.TH "SVGFEGAUSSIANBLURELEMENT.EDGEMODE" "3JS" "March 11, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
SVGFEGaussianBlurElement.edgeMode \- SVGFEGaussianBlurElement: edgeMode
property
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]edgeMode\f[B]\f[R] read\-only property of the
\f[CR]SVGFEGaussianBlurElement\f[R] interface determines what color
values to use when the blur needs to sample pixels beyond the edge of
the input image.
It reflects the \f[CR]edgeMode\f[R] attribute of the given
\f[CR]<feGaussianBlur>\f[R] element.
.PP
Its value is one of the \f[CR]SVG_EDGEMODE_*\f[R] constants defined on
the \f[CR]SVGFEGaussianBlurElement\f[R] interface.
.SH VALUE
An \f[CR]SVGAnimatedEnumeration\f[R] object.
The \f[CR]baseVal\f[R] property of this object contains one of the
following values:
.TP
\f[B]0\f[R]
Represents \f[CR]SVG_EDGEMODE_UNKNOWN\f[R], which means that the
\f[CR]edgeMode\f[R] attribute has a value other than the predefined
keywords.
.TP
\f[B]1\f[R]
Represents \f[CR]SVG_EDGEMODE_DUPLICATE\f[R], which means that the input
image is extended along each of its borders as necessary by duplicating
the color values at the given edge of the input image.
.TP
\f[B]2\f[R]
Represents \f[CR]SVG_EDGEMODE_WRAP\f[R], which means that the input
image is extended by taking the color values from the opposite edge of
the image.
.TP
\f[B]3\f[R]
Represents \f[CR]SVG_EDGEMODE_NONE\f[R], which means that the input
image is extended with pixel values of zero for the R, G, B, and A
channels.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Accessing the \f[CR]edgeMode\f[R] property
.IP
.EX
<\f[B]svg\f[R]
  viewBox=\(dq0 0 200 200\(dq
  width=\(dq300\(dq
  height=\(dq300\(dq
  xmlns=\(dqhttp://www.w3.org/2000/svg\(dq>
  <\f[B]defs\f[R]>
    <\f[B]filter\f[R] id=\(dqblur\-filter\(dq>
      <\f[B]feGaussianBlur\f[R] in=\(dqSourceGraphic\(dq stdDeviation=\(dq5\(dq />
    </\f[B]filter\f[R]>
  </\f[B]defs\f[R]>
  <\f[B]rect\f[R]
    x=\(dq20\(dq
    y=\(dq20\(dq
    width=\(dq160\(dq
    height=\(dq160\(dq
    fill=\(dqrebeccapurple\(dq
    filter=\(dqurl(#blur\-filter)\(dq />
</\f[B]svg\f[R]>
<\f[B]output\f[R]></\f[B]output\f[R]>
.EE
.PP
We can access the \f[CR]edgeMode\f[R] property to read the current
value:
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] gaussianBlur = document.querySelector(\(dqfeGaussianBlur\(dq);
\f[B]const\f[R] log = document.querySelector(\(dqoutput\(dq);

\f[B]if\f[R] (gaussianBlur.edgeMode) {
  \f[I]// Default edgeMode for feGaussianBlur is \(dqnone\(dq (3)\f[R]
  log.textContent = \(gaedgeMode.baseVal: ${gaussianBlur.edgeMode.baseVal}\(ga;
} \f[B]else\f[R] {
  log.textContent = \(dqedgeMode is not supported in this browser\(dq;
}
.EE
